         "step": 1,
         "text": "The inner expression is \\( u = 4 x - \\frac{15}{2} \\), with \\( u' = 4 \\), and \\( \\frac{d}{du}\\arcsin u = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}} \\).",
         "rule_named": "inverse trigonometric derivative with the chain rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the product rule and the chain rule, \\( h'(x) = \\frac{24 x^{2}}{\\sqrt{1 - \\left(4 x - \\frac{15}{2}\\right)^{2}}} + 12 x \\arcsin{\\left(4 x - \\frac{15}{2} \\right)} \\).",
         "rule_named": "product rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At x = 2, \\( u = \\frac{1}{2} \\) and \\( u' = 4 \\), so \\( h'(2) = 4 \\pi + 64 \\sqrt{3} \\).",
